    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I tried to stay consistent with our current way to apply conditional theme key. You'll get this in the dom: \n\n``` html\n<button class=\"ais-RefinementList__showMore ais-RefinementList__showMoreDisabled\" disabled>Show more</button>\n<!-- or -->\n<button class=\"ais-RefinementList__showMore\">Show more</button>\n```\n\nIf we change the way to compute theme here, It would be better to do it everywhere no? And since I believe that we will remove soon the react-themeable part, we would need a new way to compute classnames so maybe it's better to wait?   \n",
    "commit_id": "f862c8e3bf89b51b66a7efc9ac9ab434583c8026",
    "created_at": "2016-10-28T13:15:39Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -80,14 +80,14 @@ class List extends Component {\n   renderShowMore() {\n     const {showMore, translate, applyTheme} = this.props;\n     const {extended} = this.state;\n-\n+    const disabled = this.props.limitMin >= this.props.items.length;\n     if (!showMore) {\n       return null;\n     }\n \n     return (\n       <button\n-        {...applyTheme('showMore', 'showMore')}\n+        {...applyTheme('showMore', 'showMore', disabled && 'showMoreDisabled')}",
